sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as Sari / Budi<br/>(chat POST)
    participant RUN as runner.go<br/>composeAgent + ReAct
    participant G as Intent gate<br/>(cheap model, 1.5s max, fail-open)
    participant MS as memory tool<br/>(search fan-out)
    participant STO as Postgres<br/>hybrid indexes over<br/>events + notes + raw
    participant A as Atlas<br/>(eino ChatModelAgent)

    U->>RUN: turn arrives
    RUN->>RUN: compose working memory (transcript + cores)
    RUN->>G: "does this turn need deep memory? which stores?"
    alt self-contained
        G-->>RUN: pass-through - zero added latency
        RUN->>A: ReAct with working memory only
    else needs memory
        G-->>RUN: route: which of (timeline, graph, HDM)
        RUN->>MS: 3 concurrent agentic searches<br/>(LLM tool-loops, agent-set filters:<br/>time window / tag / source / speaker)
        MS->>STO: hybrid retrieval (embedding + lexical, RRF k=60)<br/>temporal queries: rerank skipped
        MS->>STO: OPEN raw session_events on demand<br/>(only opened rows become citable)
        MS-->>RUN: grounded candidates + opened set O
        alt O empty
            RUN->>A: inject nothing - agent may still search itself - <br/>OG abstention = no fabricated context
        else
            RUN->>A: inject candidates, each citation = source_event_id,<br/>single confidence, C subset of O
        end
        A-->>U: grounded answer -  every claim traceable to an event id
    end
